WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.160
This is the iPhone Duo,
Apple's first foldable iPhone.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.720
As someone who's intentional with their
devices and optimizes them for productivity

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.439
and reducing doom scrolling,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.080
I think that this is the best
device that they have ever made.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.080
I've been using the iPhone
Duo for the past week,

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.180
and it's clear that this phone isn't made
for everyone, but for a certain group of

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.300
people, this is the perfect device.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.520
The reason I say that is because
this phone isn't without compromise.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.520
For example, it's slightly less
ergonomic to hold one-handed.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.100
There are non-pro cameras.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:32.739
But what you're getting is essentially a
mini computer that you can fold up and put

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.820
into your pocket, and that's the
way that I think about this phone.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.200
The form factor of any device
dictates how you're going to use it,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.620
and this form factor really lends
itself to being a productivity device.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.940
Personally, I love how this form factor
is less ergonomic for short-form video.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.740
You're less likely to doom scroll on it,
and it's amazing for productivity apps.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.920
So in this video, I want to share my
experience using the iPhone Duo with the lens

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.820
of productivity and productivity apps.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.800
So I'll share with you my setup, the different
accessories that I've tested and used

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:01.540
with this,

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.140
and also compare with my experience using

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.800
the Samsung Galaxy Z Fold, which is
Android's premier foldable device.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.480
I've been using that for the past two months
for app development, and so I also want

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.580
to share my experience

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.680
comparing that with this phone.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.440
So first off, let's
talk about the display.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:22.720
My initial impression when I first
booted this up is that the display looks

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.380
absolutely incredible.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.020
So I've been a fan of matte
screen protectors for a long time.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.660
I put matte screen protectors on almost
all my devices or try to get the nano

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.280
texture display for my MacBook
and also the studio display.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:39.340
And the reason why I really like matte
screens is because it feels more calm and

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.860
more intentional to use your device.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.320
Like, it's less stimulating.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.760
There's less light, it feels like,
that's, like, coming into your eyes,

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.340
and I feel the same way when
it comes to this inner display.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.500
It just looks incredible with
all the apps and reading text

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.880
on this matte display,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.720
and I don't feel like there's any sort
of quality loss when it comes to watching

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.720
content as well. Like, when I watch
a movie on this, it looks, like,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.520
extremely high fidelity

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:05.360
and similar to my MacBook
or studio display.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:09.760
The front display is normally glossy, but
for consistency, I also got a matte screen

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.940
protector for the front.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:11.540
So

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.360
now, both the front and inside
are matte screen protected.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:18.780
If you compare that with the Z Fold 8, so
this is the premier Android foldable, it

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:19.540
has a

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.420
glossy screen on the inside,

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.080
and I feel like it just gives
it a kind of, like, a cheap,

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.960
cheap look. Like, it looks

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.400
almost like plastic

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.340
from different angles.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.740
Apparently, the matte screen is just a
screen protector, so over time, as the crease

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.980
gets more apparent, you can actually
get it replaced at the Apple Store.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.980
But that was pretty surprising to me
because no matter how I look at it, it looks

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:41.980
perfectly

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.120
attached,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.160
and you can't really tell at all
that it is a screen protector.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.120
With the Galaxy Z Fold 8,

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.080
even though it is a glossy screen,
this is also a screen protector.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:52.920
And

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.560
at least on my device, it's super obvious
because it's not even properly aligned.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.140
It's,

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.180
it's actually misaligned
for a production device.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.440
So I feel like with the iPhone, they just
have a lot higher attention to detail.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.000
In terms of accessories, I feel
like there are a few accessories

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:12.240
that really complete this product,
and the first is the Apple Pencil.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.600
In the current version of iOS, you
can connect it to an Apple Pencil,

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.980
and I didn't really think
I would use Apple Pencil.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.180
I didn't think I would
really have a stylus,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.500
use my phone like that.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:24.320
But surprisingly, it's really
nice to use as a cursor.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.640
So it works like a regular cursor.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.220
You can open up different apps.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.040
You can draw on it, and
it's super responsive.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.880
Uh, when I use it on the front screen,
it feels like I'm using a digital pocket

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:33.840
journal, so

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:34.600
this

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.760
potentially replaces my pocket notebook.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.960
It also attaches magnetically to the
side, so that just makes me feel like

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.920
maybe they are going to come out with a
smaller Apple Pencil, or maybe it's just

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.140
supposed to be like that.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.200
I'm not sure. I kind of wish there was
a more ergonomic way to carry this, but

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.280
I do have this pocket in
my jeans where it fits

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.600
on the side, so that's where
I've been putting it for now.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.260
One app that I found that is pretty nice
to use with the Apple Pencil is this one

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.000
called TypeDraw. So yeah, check this out.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:02.560
So

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:07.100
this is like a journal that you can
open up into an actual notebook,

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.780
and you can sketch in here.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.840
You can type in here
with a handwritten font,

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.180
you can write shopping lists.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:17.319
And I think this is potentially a super
underrated app that you can use to replace

00:04:17.339 --> 00:04:19.939
and have a di- digital journaling setup.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.179
You can even attach photos and annotate,

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.560
which is really nice.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.640
So yeah, I've been testing this app out,
and it's pretty cool to use with the Apple

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:30.140
Pencil. Along with the official
Apple Pencil, I also tried the

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.800
Apple Folio case, which is more of a MagSafe
accessory, I would say, than an actual

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:38.860
case. I think the idea with this case is
basically to encourage you to only use the

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.740
inner display because the front display
is covered, and it's actually kind of hard

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.580
to use the front display
when you have this case on.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.940
So I kind of like the idea.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.080
It forces you to be more intentional, but

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.340
I wanted to also use the
front display, so I ended up

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.840
choosing something else.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:53.400
The

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.900
one accessory that I found that is really
useful to use with the iPhone Duo is

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.120
this MagSafe accessory.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.120
So this is a MagSafe ring made by ALUMU.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.720
I don't think I've ever
said that alo- out loud, but

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.020
it's made by ALUMU,

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.180
and

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.040
it's

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.380
a ring that you can put
your finger in on the back.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.340
And I think it really helps you hold the
phone in a way more ergonomic position.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.040
So

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.020
with this setup,

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.560
I can reach every corner
of the iPhone Duo.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:26.980
I can easily reach the volume buttons,
and I can also easily unlock the phone

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.840
one-handed. It also works in every
orientation, so whether you're using it

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.200
front vertical

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.340
or front

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.740
horizontal,

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.160
you can put your finger in the back.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.100
And the same if you're having it
unfolded horizontal or unfolded

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.860
vertical, like, this ring
works in the same orientation.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:43.440
And

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.500
this ring is also nice
because it expands into a

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:50.000
kickstand, so you can
also put it on the desk

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:54.480
and watch a video. And this back part is
also magnetic, so it also sticks to, like,

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:58.540
gym equipment or anything that is
magnetic, like a fridge, for example.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.140
Yeah, I'm not, I'm not affiliated with
this accessory at all, but I think it

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.460
significantly improved my experience
with holding and using the iPhone Duo.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:10.180
The kickstand is also really convenient
for when you want to use it like a mini

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.140
computer, like when you
want to watch some content

00:06:12.248 --> 00:06:16.848
Or when you want to actually use a keyboard,
which leads me to the next accessory

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:17.608
that I want to share.

00:06:17.628 --> 00:06:20.568
So I think the experience of
using the iPhone Duo is really

00:06:20.668 --> 00:06:24.388
elevated when you use it with a folding
keyboard or a portable keyboard.

00:06:24.408 --> 00:06:27.428
It actually feels like you
are using a mini computer.

00:06:27.448 --> 00:06:30.848
In the latest iOS update, they have full
support for a portable keyboard and a

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:35.708
portable mouse, so you could literally have
a cursor and mouse and be navigating on

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:40.168
the iPhone Duo. If you do any sort of work
like prompting agents, writing emails, or

00:06:40.188 --> 00:06:44.408
even writing YouTube videos, it's really
nice because you don't have to have your

00:06:44.428 --> 00:06:47.328
whole computer set up just
to do some basic work.

00:06:47.348 --> 00:06:50.248
The keyboard that I'm using is made
by this company called iClever.

00:06:50.268 --> 00:06:52.868
I also talked about this
in a previous video before.

00:06:52.888 --> 00:06:54.728
I'm also not affiliated with them at all,

00:06:54.908 --> 00:06:58.468
but I think this one is really nice because
it folds up and I can put it in my back

00:06:58.488 --> 00:07:03.928
pocket and easily go to a coffee shop
or even travel with this in my backpack.

00:07:03.948 --> 00:07:07.928
So with this keyboard setup, you could use
the basic multitasking and have a split

00:07:07.948 --> 00:07:08.568
screen,

00:07:08.768 --> 00:07:13.148
but one thing that you can do to take it
further is remote log into your computer

00:07:13.168 --> 00:07:15.128
and actually control your computer.

00:07:15.428 --> 00:07:19.228
So the app that I use for this is called
Jump Desktop, and in their latest beta,

00:07:19.248 --> 00:07:21.128
they have full support for iPhone Duo.

00:07:21.408 --> 00:07:26.768
So what that looks like is that I can, at
any time, anywhere, log into my Mac or any

00:07:26.788 --> 00:07:27.888
of my computers

00:07:28.228 --> 00:07:31.328
and be able to remote control
them with a keyboard, so

00:07:31.528 --> 00:07:34.348
I get the full desktop experience.

00:07:34.368 --> 00:07:37.888
I think this app is amazing because
it actually resizes your display to

00:07:38.028 --> 00:07:39.868
support the device you're using,

00:07:40.028 --> 00:07:44.148
so it feels like I'm actually
using macOS on my iPhone Duo.

00:07:44.168 --> 00:07:48.328
Like, it even works with the Apple
Pencil to move different windows around.

00:07:48.348 --> 00:07:51.908
It's surprisingly smooth because you can
adjust the frame rate, you can adjust the

00:07:51.928 --> 00:07:52.848
resolution.

00:07:52.948 --> 00:07:58.088
And so with this setup, I can do stuff like
basic editing, I can use my full desktop

00:07:58.108 --> 00:08:02.208
browser or any desktop applications, and
so I basically don't even need to bring a

00:08:02.228 --> 00:08:04.328
computer or iPad if I'm traveling.

00:08:04.348 --> 00:08:08.648
There's even support for Linux, so I can
remote log into my Linux computer and be

00:08:08.668 --> 00:08:12.228
able to use all marquee on my
iPhone Duo, which is super fun.

00:08:12.248 --> 00:08:13.748
In terms of the native

00:08:13.908 --> 00:08:17.488
iOS multitasking, I also
think they really made it

00:08:17.688 --> 00:08:19.188
super simple to use.

00:08:19.308 --> 00:08:24.488
Compared with Android, the multitasking
setup is really confusing and difficult to

00:08:24.508 --> 00:08:26.128
use, like there are a lot of menus.

00:08:26.228 --> 00:08:30.208
At one point, I had to watch a tutorial
just to see all the different features.

00:08:30.228 --> 00:08:33.968
Some people might say that this is a
downside, but on iOS, you can only have two

00:08:33.988 --> 00:08:37.348
apps side by side, whereas
on Android, you can have

00:08:37.648 --> 00:08:39.048
as many apps as you want, basically.

00:08:39.068 --> 00:08:41.068
You can have four apps,
like one in every corner.

00:08:41.088 --> 00:08:43.688
You can have windowed apps
that you can move around.

00:08:43.968 --> 00:08:45.888
But in my experience, it's

00:08:46.128 --> 00:08:50.148
really performative if you want to have
more than two apps open on a s- screen that

00:08:50.168 --> 00:08:54.128
is this size. So it's sort of unrealistic
to have more than two apps open, in my

00:08:54.148 --> 00:08:54.948
experience,

00:08:55.268 --> 00:08:59.468
and also it just makes it way more cluttered
and way harder to use when you have

00:08:59.808 --> 00:09:02.328
a lot more options. So

00:09:02.568 --> 00:09:05.428
I feel like they really cut options.

00:09:05.448 --> 00:09:07.068
To use it on the iPhone
Duo is super simple.

00:09:07.088 --> 00:09:08.148
You just swipe up,

00:09:08.408 --> 00:09:10.948
you wait a second, and then
you can just put it into

00:09:11.108 --> 00:09:14.188
any corner. And when you want to switch
between the left and right side, you can

00:09:14.208 --> 00:09:15.368
just switch it like that.

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:18.588
So there's also this feature when you
have two apps open that you can tap on the

00:09:18.608 --> 00:09:20.928
middle to merge the two apps.

00:09:21.088 --> 00:09:26.128
And so what that basically does is that
after that, whenever you open up any of the

00:09:26.148 --> 00:09:29.088
two apps, it will open up
two of them simultaneously.

00:09:29.388 --> 00:09:32.008
And I think this is super underrated because
there are a lot of apps where it just

00:09:32.028 --> 00:09:35.008
makes sense to have both of
them open at the same time.

00:09:35.028 --> 00:09:35.948
For example,

00:09:36.148 --> 00:09:39.388
the Camera app and the
Photos app together, or

00:09:39.508 --> 00:09:43.428
maybe you're learning a language and you
have Anki and a dictionary, or a book app

00:09:43.448 --> 00:09:44.428
and a dictionary,

00:09:44.828 --> 00:09:50.088
or even at the gym, you can have your workout
app on one side and maybe social media

00:09:50.168 --> 00:09:51.868
or Reddit on the other side.

00:09:51.888 --> 00:09:55.188
At least for me, I've been doing that a
lot and pairing different apps together.

00:09:55.208 --> 00:09:58.628
I think I also mostly use the
phone unfolded most of the time.

00:09:58.648 --> 00:10:01.488
Like, I like to use it
like a mini computer.

00:10:01.508 --> 00:10:05.648
Uh, if you regularly get on any sort of
calls, whether that's for school or work, I

00:10:05.668 --> 00:10:09.008
think this is also a really nice
setup for video conferencing.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:12.468
So on the inner display,
there is a under screen,

00:10:12.608 --> 00:10:15.288
uh, camera that you can kind of
see in different reflections.

00:10:15.308 --> 00:10:18.628
And even though the resolution on that
is pretty low, I think it really doesn't

00:10:18.648 --> 00:10:19.588
matter for

00:10:19.768 --> 00:10:23.328
video calls. Like, I've used
it, and I don't think anyone has

00:10:23.448 --> 00:10:25.628
said anything or even really cared.

00:10:25.648 --> 00:10:29.648
Uh, you still have the full resolution
camera on the back and also on the outer side

00:10:29.668 --> 00:10:30.728
of the front screen,

00:10:31.068 --> 00:10:35.808
so I think it is the correct decision to
use an under screen camera on the inside

00:10:35.828 --> 00:10:38.368
with the downside of it
being a lower quality camera.

00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:42.768
If you do take video calls, though, one
app that I found that is really useful and

00:10:42.788 --> 00:10:46.988
well supported on the iPhone Duo is this
app called Granola, who's also kindly

00:10:47.008 --> 00:10:48.068
sponsoring this video.

00:10:48.088 --> 00:10:52.048
So Granola is an application that
automatically take notes from any meeting that

00:10:52.068 --> 00:10:56.148
you're in. It can be a call
or even a real life meeting.

00:10:56.168 --> 00:10:59.948
How you use it is you just launch it when
you're in a meeting, and it will use the

00:10:59.968 --> 00:11:05.488
microphone or the audio on your computer
to automatically transcribe and summarize

00:11:05.508 --> 00:11:07.188
your call when you're done.

00:11:07.208 --> 00:11:09.948
All your calls are nicely
organized in Granola,

00:11:10.128 --> 00:11:13.288
or you can easily import them
into any app, like Obsidian.

00:11:13.308 --> 00:11:17.068
Uh, normally, if you wanted this workflow,
you would have to record the audio,

00:11:17.268 --> 00:11:20.788
then transcribe it and diarize it, and
then give it to an AI to summarize,

00:11:20.928 --> 00:11:22.508
and finally save it somewhere.

00:11:22.528 --> 00:11:25.928
Granola does all that for you automatically,
so when you're in a call, you don't

00:11:25.948 --> 00:11:27.128
have to worry about taking notes.

00:11:27.148 --> 00:11:28.748
You don't have to worry
about anything else,

00:11:28.868 --> 00:11:31.408
and you can just focus on the
thing that you're talking about.

00:11:31.428 --> 00:11:35.188
On desktop, it'll even detect when you're
in a meeting and automatically start the

00:11:35.208 --> 00:11:36.408
transcription process.

00:11:36.428 --> 00:11:39.988
What makes Granola unique is that it works
with any meeting platform, whether that's

00:11:40.008 --> 00:11:42.448
Google Meets, Discord, or Zoom,

00:11:42.748 --> 00:11:46.948
and the best part is that there is no bot
that joins the call and gives everyone

00:11:46.968 --> 00:11:51.748
pressure. Plan is free, and it covers more
than enough for most people's needs, so

00:11:51.908 --> 00:11:54.688
if you want to try it out, check out the
link in the description, and you can try it

00:11:54.708 --> 00:11:55.668
out for free.

00:11:55.868 --> 00:11:57.248
But yeah, let's get back into the video.

00:11:57.268 --> 00:12:01.068
Besides Granola, I think most of the
productivity apps that I use have been updated

00:12:01.088 --> 00:12:02.848
to support the iPhone Duo.

00:12:03.108 --> 00:12:07.928
For example, Claude I feel like really makes
good use of the real estate, so it kind

00:12:07.948 --> 00:12:09.888
of looks like the desktop app.

00:12:09.908 --> 00:12:13.228
And for example, if you're
working on a website or an app-

00:12:13.636 --> 00:12:16.956
You could have the artifact on one side,
and then you could have the chat window on

00:12:16.976 --> 00:12:17.996
the other. So

00:12:18.136 --> 00:12:20.376
this is a super ergonomic setup.

00:12:20.396 --> 00:12:23.576
For me, I do quite a lot of app
development for my app, Habits First,

00:12:23.876 --> 00:12:28.496
and so it's really nice to also use the
split screen feature to have the app on one

00:12:28.516 --> 00:12:32.716
side, and on the other, I could have the
terminal, where I could have NVim, or we

00:12:32.736 --> 00:12:35.956
could have Cloud Code
or Herder on the other.

00:12:36.336 --> 00:12:40.276
If you use Herder, also it looks
really nice on the iPhone Duo.

00:12:40.296 --> 00:12:43.396
It looks kind of like the desktop version.

00:12:43.416 --> 00:12:46.475
I use this app called Moshi
to SSH into my computer,

00:12:46.636 --> 00:12:48.516
and once I'm there, I can use

00:12:48.736 --> 00:12:49.256
pretty much anything.

00:12:49.276 --> 00:12:50.516
I can use Tmux,

00:12:50.656 --> 00:12:51.396
NVim,

00:12:51.596 --> 00:12:53.396
Herder, Cloud Code, Codex.

00:12:53.496 --> 00:12:57.236
And so I think it's a really essential
app for coding and productivity.

00:12:57.256 --> 00:13:00.796
But besides that, in terms of productivity
apps that I- I've been using on this,

00:13:00.856 --> 00:13:01.716
Obsidian

00:13:02.056 --> 00:13:04.276
seems to work pretty
well for the most part.

00:13:04.296 --> 00:13:07.796
I actually prepared this iPhone
Duo video on the iPhone Duo.

00:13:07.816 --> 00:13:10.296
Reading books on the iPhone
Duo is also really nice.

00:13:10.316 --> 00:13:13.936
It kind of feels like you have
an actual book in your hands.

00:13:13.956 --> 00:13:15.896
So in Japan, they have a standardized

00:13:16.096 --> 00:13:18.316
novel size, and it's called the Bunkobon,

00:13:18.515 --> 00:13:19.876
and it kind of feels like

00:13:20.076 --> 00:13:23.876
this iPhone Duo. You can read the book
partially folded like this, so it kind of

00:13:23.896 --> 00:13:25.736
actually feels like you're reading a book.

00:13:25.996 --> 00:13:29.436
But in most cases, I feel like reading
it completely flat is more ergonomic.

00:13:29.456 --> 00:13:32.956
The exceptions where I think it would
make sense to read it like this is

00:13:33.076 --> 00:13:36.316
maybe you're on the train, and you don't
want the person next to you to see what

00:13:36.336 --> 00:13:38.816
you're reading, or maybe
there's, like, sun,

00:13:38.956 --> 00:13:43.576
and you're trying to block the sun out,
which has also come in handy for me before.

00:13:43.596 --> 00:13:45.876
The app that I use for
books is called Still,

00:13:46.036 --> 00:13:50.696
and it connects to my self-hosted library,
so it syncs across all my different

00:13:50.716 --> 00:13:53.896
devices. I've been trying
to read more lately, and

00:13:54.056 --> 00:13:56.756
my app, Habits First, has
really been helpful for that.

00:13:56.776 --> 00:14:00.596
So I can set, like, a number of pages
that I want to read before my other apps

00:14:00.616 --> 00:14:05.476
unlock, or also a number of minutes I
want to read per day before my other apps

00:14:05.496 --> 00:14:08.116
unlock. But besides purely

00:14:08.576 --> 00:14:12.356
stuff for productivity, I think this form
factor and setup is also really nice for

00:14:12.376 --> 00:14:15.116
watching movies and videos, especially

00:14:15.216 --> 00:14:17.796
if you're traveling or you're
on public transportation.

00:14:17.816 --> 00:14:21.476
But I would say that it's probably not
worth buying the iPhone Duo if your primary

00:14:21.496 --> 00:14:25.056
use case is to watch
videos or movies because

00:14:25.396 --> 00:14:27.856
for most 16 by nine videos,

00:14:27.996 --> 00:14:31.556
you're probably not going to get that much
more screen real estate compared to just

00:14:31.576 --> 00:14:35.036
watching it on your phone because of
the black bars on the top and bottom.

00:14:35.416 --> 00:14:39.676
And so with movies at least, you can
only really get the best experience

00:14:39.856 --> 00:14:44.196
if you're watching an IMAX movie,
which is closer to this aspect ratio,

00:14:44.356 --> 00:14:46.816
and those are kind of rare.

00:14:46.836 --> 00:14:50.656
So I think if your primary use case is
watching videos or movies, you might as well

00:14:50.676 --> 00:14:54.576
get an iPad or an iPhone Pro Max.

00:14:54.596 --> 00:14:57.976
Uh, in terms of gaming, I haven't gamed
that much on the iPhone, but I think it's

00:14:57.996 --> 00:15:01.916
kind of worth mentioning because there
has been a pretty interesting effort to

00:15:01.936 --> 00:15:05.676
reverse engineer games and make
them compatible on the iPhone Duo.

00:15:05.696 --> 00:15:06.236
Like

00:15:06.376 --> 00:15:11.176
for example, someone reverse engineered
Factorio to be playable on the iPhone Duo,

00:15:11.436 --> 00:15:15.996
and there's also a GitHub repo where you
can play Nintendo Switch games on the

00:15:16.016 --> 00:15:18.176
iPhone Duo if you had purchased them,

00:15:18.356 --> 00:15:20.736
so I think that's pretty interesting.

00:15:20.756 --> 00:15:23.096
There's also this app called
Delta where you can play

00:15:23.316 --> 00:15:28.196
NDS games in this nostalgic form factor,
so I can definitely see myself playing with

00:15:28.216 --> 00:15:32.096
that sometimes if I'm on a flight or I'm
waiting for something or listening to a

00:15:32.116 --> 00:15:33.456
podcast. And

00:15:33.616 --> 00:15:37.256
this setup could also be good for turn-based
games, like maybe if you play chess or

00:15:37.276 --> 00:15:40.816
Polytopia, you could have it on one
side, and you could have a video call or

00:15:40.836 --> 00:15:42.456
something else on the other side.

00:15:42.476 --> 00:15:45.256
But overall, how does
this device compare to

00:15:45.556 --> 00:15:47.696
the other things on the
market right now, like

00:15:47.876 --> 00:15:49.936
the premier Galaxy Z Fold8?

00:15:50.256 --> 00:15:55.276
So having used the Samsung Galaxy Z Fold8
for the past two months, I would say that

00:15:55.296 --> 00:15:59.036
these two devices are really not comparable
at all, even though they are both

00:15:59.056 --> 00:16:00.776
premium foldable devices.

00:16:00.796 --> 00:16:04.156
Personally, I found that the iPhone Duo has
a better user experience in almost every

00:16:04.176 --> 00:16:04.816
way.

00:16:05.176 --> 00:16:11.196
I encounter a lot more bugs on the
Android, and it feels way more choppy and

00:16:11.216 --> 00:16:12.256
disjointed

00:16:12.456 --> 00:16:15.116
as an experience. It
feels like multiple teams

00:16:15.216 --> 00:16:16.716
working separately,

00:16:16.856 --> 00:16:18.336
putting their stuff together.

00:16:18.376 --> 00:16:22.136
And with the iPhone Duo, I can feel that
they probably tested all the different

00:16:22.156 --> 00:16:26.196
things that Android can do, but they
decided to cut different features so that it

00:16:26.216 --> 00:16:29.676
has a more streamlined and smooth

00:16:29.796 --> 00:16:34.216
user experience. It also feels like iOS
developers, as a culture, feel way more

00:16:34.236 --> 00:16:35.335
motivated to

00:16:35.495 --> 00:16:36.676
adapt their apps

00:16:36.776 --> 00:16:38.336
to support the latest iPhones,

00:16:38.436 --> 00:16:42.036
whereas it doesn't really seem
to be the case with Android.

00:16:42.056 --> 00:16:45.616
So yeah, I think that's why almost all
the apps that I use regularly have already

00:16:45.636 --> 00:16:47.916
been updated to support the iPhone Duo.

00:16:47.936 --> 00:16:53.276
One thing I will say that Android is much
further ahead than Apple is the idea of

00:16:53.296 --> 00:16:56.296
using your phone as your only device.

00:16:56.496 --> 00:17:01.796
So with the Samsung Galaxy Z Fold8, you
can plug it into a monitor, and it kind of

00:17:01.816 --> 00:17:02.636
becomes

00:17:02.936 --> 00:17:06.796
a actual computer. So you get
Windows, you get a taskbar,

00:17:07.076 --> 00:17:08.796
and you can actually move stuff around.

00:17:08.816 --> 00:17:09.376
And

00:17:09.496 --> 00:17:12.976
I think that would be pretty amazing
if the iPhone also supported that.

00:17:12.996 --> 00:17:14.236
Like, imagine you had

00:17:14.596 --> 00:17:15.516
iOS

00:17:15.736 --> 00:17:19.816
when it's folded, you had iPad OS when
it's unfolded, and then when you plugged it

00:17:19.836 --> 00:17:23.716
in, you had macOS. That would definitely
cannibalize their sales, but I think that

00:17:23.736 --> 00:17:24.436
would be

00:17:24.596 --> 00:17:26.456
the most amazing device ever.

00:17:26.476 --> 00:17:27.476
But yeah, in terms of

00:17:27.776 --> 00:17:31.836
biggest concerns that I had before I got
this or things I wish I knew before I got

00:17:31.856 --> 00:17:32.416
this,

00:17:32.776 --> 00:17:33.916
when I watched

00:17:34.016 --> 00:17:36.196
a lot of the reviews by
different tech reviewers,

00:17:36.456 --> 00:17:40.216
one of the biggest concerns that I
had was that it would be a really

00:17:40.316 --> 00:17:43.736
unsmooth experience with using
different apps on the iPhone.

00:17:43.756 --> 00:17:45.876
But having used this for the past week,

00:17:46.076 --> 00:17:48.796
I can say that that hasn't
really been the case at all.

00:17:48.816 --> 00:17:51.956
I think with those videos,
really what's happening is that

00:17:52.096 --> 00:17:55.216
they were using the phone
before anyone else had

00:17:55.356 --> 00:17:56.556
access to the phone.

00:17:56.616 --> 00:17:59.896
So of course, all the apps that they tried
are not going to be optimized for the

00:17:59.916 --> 00:18:03.536
iPhone Duo. But now that the phone has
been out, most of the apps that I use have

00:18:03.556 --> 00:18:08.308
been updated, and even my app, Habits
First, has been updated- This week

00:18:08.428 --> 00:18:13.208
for the iPhone Duo. And also a lot of apps
on my phone, I think it genuinely doesn't

00:18:13.228 --> 00:18:14.668
even matter if they update it or not.

00:18:14.688 --> 00:18:16.268
Like for example, Tailscale

00:18:16.468 --> 00:18:21.008
or Anki, it doesn't really bother me at
all whether or not it's optimized for the

00:18:21.028 --> 00:18:24.768
iPhone Duo. I can just use it in the
split screen or front screen mode.

00:18:24.788 --> 00:18:29.048
Another concern that I had was whether or
not touch ID would be significantly worse

00:18:29.068 --> 00:18:32.948
than face ID. And at least for me, I
haven't found that to be an issue at all.

00:18:32.968 --> 00:18:37.208
It is slightly slower than face ID, so it
kind of forces you to be more intentional

00:18:37.228 --> 00:18:38.328
with your phone. So

00:18:38.588 --> 00:18:41.628
you hit the button, you wait
a second, and then it unlocks.

00:18:41.648 --> 00:18:44.968
But if that bothers you, there's also
some pretty simple solutions for that.

00:18:45.168 --> 00:18:50.568
One is you can actually add the side of
your finger as a fingerprint, like right,

00:18:50.668 --> 00:18:51.588
like right here.

00:18:51.808 --> 00:18:52.388
So

00:18:52.768 --> 00:18:54.828
as soon as you pull the
phone out of your pocket

00:18:54.988 --> 00:18:58.388
in this formation, it'll just
automatically unlock, and

00:18:58.568 --> 00:19:00.768
I found that to be super fast.

00:19:01.028 --> 00:19:04.508
Another solution is if you
use an Apple Watch like me,

00:19:04.788 --> 00:19:08.028
it basically unlocks
maybe even faster than

00:19:08.368 --> 00:19:09.768
face ID, so

00:19:09.928 --> 00:19:11.688
that essentially solves that issue.

00:19:11.708 --> 00:19:13.528
And personally, I don't
really miss face ID.

00:19:13.548 --> 00:19:16.348
I like touch ID because there
were a lot of times where

00:19:16.648 --> 00:19:20.708
I'm using my phone, like lying down on a
sofa or in bed and it doesn't unlock, or

00:19:20.908 --> 00:19:22.248
maybe I am

00:19:22.548 --> 00:19:25.148
wearing a mask or sunglasses
and it doesn't unlock.

00:19:25.168 --> 00:19:27.708
Like that's happened many
times before in the past.

00:19:27.728 --> 00:19:30.808
So yeah, final verdict
and who this phone is for.

00:19:30.828 --> 00:19:34.048
The iPhone Duo is amazing if you
want a computer in your pocket.

00:19:34.068 --> 00:19:38.408
It transforms your regular phone from
something built for short form video and doom

00:19:38.428 --> 00:19:42.428
scrolling into something that's built for
productivity, a foldable computer that you

00:19:42.448 --> 00:19:43.888
can put in your pocket.

00:19:43.908 --> 00:19:47.888
You can legitimately do work for long
periods of time using this device,

00:19:48.068 --> 00:19:51.948
and in many cases, it can be
a full on laptop replacement.

00:19:51.968 --> 00:19:55.848
I've found in using this device that it's
given me a better relationship with my

00:19:55.868 --> 00:20:00.528
phone, whether that's with taking notes,
journaling, studying, or even studying Anki

00:20:00.548 --> 00:20:04.828
cards. I also think this is one of the most
fun devices that Apple has released in a

00:20:04.848 --> 00:20:06.088
long time. That's it for this video.

00:20:06.108 --> 00:20:08.588
Let me know in the comments
below, would you try

00:20:08.868 --> 00:20:11.168
an iPhone Duo? Would you
switch to an iPhone Duo?

00:20:11.368 --> 00:20:13.968
And if you have any questions about the
iPhone Duo, you can let me know in the

00:20:13.988 --> 00:20:16.948
comments below. I'll try to
respond to all the comments,

00:20:17.108 --> 00:20:18.348
and that's it for this one.

00:20:18.368 --> 00:20:19.348
I'll see you next video.

00:20:19.368 --> 00:20:20.188
Let's get it.

